---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Sources from "../components/Sources.astro";
import Plates from "../components/Plates.astro";
import Lightbox from "../components/Lightbox.astro";
import s from "../data/seget.json";
import v from "../data/seget-voce.json";
import SegetArms from "../components/SegetArms.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
---
<Base title="Seget, and Crete" eyebrow="The other Istrian branch"
      dek="A published monograph on an estate near Umag says something no family account here had: that there were two branches of this family in Istria — one seated at Gologorica, the other at Umag and Seget — and that the second came out of Crete.">

<section class="blk">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>The <em>stancija</em> at Seget, a few kilometres south of Umag, is the subject of a 2019 monograph published by the Croatian Ministry of Culture. Its second chapter is titled <em>Obitelj de Franceschi i Seget u povijesnim izvorima</em> — the de Franceschi family and Seget in the historical sources — and it states the thing plainly:</p>
    <p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:19px;font-style:italic;color:var(--ink);border-left:2px solid var(--terra);padding-left:20px">“There were two branches of the family in Istria, one seated at Gologorica, and the other at Umag and Seget. Family archives survive from both.”</p>
    <p>The Umag branch reached Istria by fleeing <strong>Crete after the Candian War of 1669</strong>, when the Ottomans took the island from Venice. Half a century later they bought the estate.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <h2>How the estate came to them</h2>
  <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:20px">
    <table><tbody>{s.timeline.map(([y,t])=>(
      <tr><td class="m" style="width:64px">{y}</td><td>{t}</td></tr>))}</tbody></table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <h2>The household</h2>
  <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:20px">
    <table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th class="m">Dates</th><th>What the sources say</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{s.people.map(([n,d,w])=>(<tr><td>{n}</td><td class="m">{d}</td><td>{w}</td></tr>))}</tbody></table>
  </div>
  <div class="grid g2" style="margin-top:24px">
    <div class="panel"><div class="lab">Marc'Antonio &amp; Crissulla's eleven children</div>
      <p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--ink-2);margin-top:10px">{s.children_marcantonio.join(" · ")}</p></div>
    <div class="panel"><div class="lab">Alvise &amp; Francesca Borella's six</div>
      <p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--ink-2);margin-top:10px">{s.children_alvise.join(" · ")}</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="prose" style="margin-top:26px">
    <p>Two details carry the Cretan origin without needing to argue it. Marc'Antonio's wife is <strong>Crissulla Marulli</strong> — Chrysoula Marouli, a Greek name, not an Istrian one. And his son <strong>Alvise</strong> is recorded in the family's own genealogy as <em>Dragomanno alla Porta ottomana</em>: dragoman, the interpreter-diplomat, at the Ottoman court. A family two generations out of Crete would have the Greek and the Turkish to do that work.</p>
    <p>The estate itself still carries their marks. A portal cut with <strong>1724</strong>; the stone well-head in front of the house cut with <strong>1732</strong> and the initials <strong>M A · F</strong>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <h2>Two family archives, and two family trees</h2>
  <p class="dek">This is the most valuable thing on the page. Both branches deposited their papers, and both are catalogued.</p>
  <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:22px">
    <table><thead><tr><th class="m">Fond</th><th>Where</th><th>What it holds</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{s.archives.map(([f,w,h])=>(<tr><td class="m">{f}</td><td>{w}</td><td>{h}</td></tr>))}</tbody></table>
  </div>
  <div class="note" style="margin-top:26px">Two genealogies of this family already exist in Croatian state archives — one drawn up about <b>1896</b> at Rijeka giving every member with birth, death and marriage dates, and one drawn up in <b>1927</b> at Pazin giving the male line. Neither has been read for this archive. Between them they would almost certainly settle several of the questions still open on the research log.</div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <h2>What Carlo's own book adds</h2>
  <p class="dek">Reading <em>L'Istria: note storiche</em> (1879) for the family rather than for the history turns up four things.</p>
  <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:20px">
    <table><tbody>{s.carlo.map(([y,t])=>(
      <tr><td class="m" style="width:64px">{y}</td><td>{t}</td></tr>))}</tbody></table>
  </div>
  <div class="prose" style="margin-top:24px">
    <p>The first is worth sitting with. Carlo De Franceschi spent his life arguing for the Italian character of Istria. In the middle of a passage on when Slavic place-names begin to appear in the record, he notes that in <strong>1102</strong> one finds <em>Golgoriza</em> — and adds the Italian name in brackets, <em>Moncalvo</em>. It is the earliest documented mention of his own birthplace, and he is recording it as evidence of Slavic settlement.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="cap">{s.source}</p>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <h2>A county in Crete, and a shipwreck coming home</h2>
  <p class="dek">A 2020 feature in <em>la Voce del popolo</em> — the Italian-language daily of Rijeka — sets out the Seghetto family's own account of itself, and it explains what the branch was doing in Crete in the first place.</p>
  <div class="prose" style="margin-top:22px">
    <p>They were not merchants there. They held a county. In the Veneto-Turkish war of <strong>1538</strong> the counts de Franceschi defended the Cretan ports of Calus, Lemiores and Sabionera with <strong>nine hundred vassals</strong> of their own county, at their own expense — and in 1581 the Duke of Candia, Marcantonio Querini, confirmed them the privileges of <em>mero et misto imperio</em>, the delegated power to administer justice, for services rendered <em>“nelle più ardue ricorrenze, col somministrar gente, haveri et cavalli, esponendo ancora se stessi ai rischi di guerra per la difesa del Regno”</em> — in the hardest of times, supplying men, goods and horses, and exposing themselves to the risks of war for the defence of the Kingdom.</p>
    <p class="note" style="margin-top:14px">{v.wreck}</p>
    <p>That is the sentence the Seget story turns on. The family did not simply relocate. They were evacuated by Morosini's galleys with the other Venetian families of Candia, and the fleet that carried them was wrecked in a storm on the way home. The people who bought the Umago estate fifty-one years later were the ones who got out of the water.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:24px">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th class="m">When</th><th>The honours, as the family records them</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{v.honours.map(([y, t]) => <tr><td class="m">{y}</td><td>{t}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class="note" style="margin-top:22px">The 474 story is a nobiliary origin legend of the kind every counted house in Italy acquired, and it is set out here as one. What is not legend is that the family went on giving the name <strong>Ferramondo</strong> to its sons: a Ferramondo de Franceschi was a commissioner of Umago between 1918 and 1945. A family that keeps naming children after its own myth is telling you something true about itself, whatever the myth is worth.</div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <h2>The arms on the tympanum</h2>
  <div class="grid g2" style="margin-top:24px;align-items:start">
    <SegetArms />
    <div class="prose">
      <p>The <em>Blasonario Giuliano</em> lists a second family of this name whose arms it can only give as <em>“Di … al leone di …”</em> — a lion, tinctures unrecorded. The Seghetto façade supplies them: <strong>troncato di azzurro e d'oro al leone rampante al naturale</strong>, per fess azure and or.</p>
      <p>{v.trade}</p>
      <p>Two men of standing are recorded as guests of the house: {v.guests.map((g, i) => <><strong>{g[0]}</strong> ({g[1]}), {g[2]}{i < v.guests.length - 1 ? " And " : ""}</>)}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <h2>How the house was built, and what happened to the library</h2>
  <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:18px">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th class="m">When</th><th>What</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{v.estate.map(([y, t]) => <tr><td class="m">{y}</td><td>{t}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class="prose" style="margin-top:24px">
    <p>The east wing held <strong>over four thousand volumes</strong>, bought from the booksellers of Trieste, Piran, Buje and Poreč, and beside them the family archive — held by some scholars to be one of the richest libraries in Istria. Both were destroyed in the twentieth century, and the room that held them was cut up into smaller rooms.</p>
    <p>Set that against the <a href={u("/research-log/")}>research log</a>, where two surviving de Franceschi family archives — HR-DARI-382 at Rijeka and HR-DAPA-828 at Pazin — are listed as the largest untouched source in this project. The Seghetto library is the counter-example, and the reason to write those letters now rather than later.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <h2>The two branches, and what they did</h2>
  <p class="dek">The family split. One branch held the farms of Seghetto, Giubba and Spinel; the other, the Umago branch, held Rosazzo, Macalè — formerly Casoni — and Carsette.</p>
  <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:18px">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Who</th><th class="m">When</th><th>What</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{v.offices.map(([n, y, t]) => <tr><td>{n}</td><td class="m">{y}</td><td>{t}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="cap" style="margin-top:18px">Source: {v.source}</p>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <h2>{s.voce.heading}</h2>
  <p class="dek" style="margin-top:10px">{s.voce.lead}</p>

  <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:22px">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th class="m">When</th><th>What</th><th>As the article gives it</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{s.voce.origins.map(o => (
        <tr>
          <td class="m">{o.y}</td>
          <td>{o.key ? <strong>{o.t}</strong> : o.t}{o.lore && <><br /><span class="chip lore" style="padding:2px 7px;font-size:10px">Family lore</span></>}</td>
          <td>{o.w}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="one" style="border-left-color:var(--terra);margin-top:32px">
    <div class="lab">The arms over the door</div>
    <h3>{s.voce.house.heading}</h3>
    <p>{s.voce.house.text}</p>
    <p class="qit" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-style:italic;font-size:18px;margin-top:16px">“{s.voce.house.blazon}”</p>
    <p style="margin-top:10px">{s.voce.house.blazonEn}</p>
    <p class="cap" style="margin-top:12px">{s.voce.house.rest}</p>
  </div>

  <div class="one" style="margin-top:20px">
    <div class="lab">Santa Costanza</div>
    <h3>{s.voce.chapel.heading}</h3>
    <p>{s.voce.chapel.text}</p>
  </div>

  <h3 style="font-size:24px;margin-top:38px">{s.voce.public.heading}</h3>
  <p class="dek" style="margin-top:8px">{s.voce.public.branches}</p>
  <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:16px">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Who</th><th class="m">When</th><th>What</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{s.voce.public.rows.map(([who, when, what]) => (
        <tr><td>{who}</td><td class="m">{when || "—"}</td><td>{what}</td></tr>
      ))}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="prose" style="margin-top:18px">{s.voce.public.guests}</p>
  <p class="cap" style="margin-top:16px">{s.voce.caveat}</p>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <h2>{s.diet.heading}</h2>
  <p class="dek" style="margin-top:10px">{s.diet.lead}</p>

  <blockquote class="qz" style="margin-top:20px">
    <p style="font-style:italic">{s.diet.quote}</p>
    <p class="cap" style="margin-top:12px">{s.diet.en}</p>
  </blockquote>

  <h3 style="font-size:22px;margin-top:30px">What he does in that one sitting</h3>
  <ul class="prose" style="display:block;margin-top:10px">
    {s.diet.roles.map(r => <li style="margin:.45em 0">{r}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <div class="one" style="border-left-color:var(--terra);margin-top:26px">
    <div class="lab">On the same order paper</div>
    <h3>{s.diet.gallignana.heading}</h3>
    <p>{s.diet.gallignana.text}</p>
  </div>

  <div class="one" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="lab">Identity</div>
    <h3>{s.diet.who.heading}</h3>
    <p>{s.diet.who.text}</p>
    <p class="cap" style="margin-top:12px">{s.diet.who.caution}</p>
  </div>

  <div class="one" style="border-left-color:var(--accent);margin-top:22px">
    <div class="lab">Confirmed</div>
    <h3>{s.diet.confirmed.heading}</h3>
    <p class="qit" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-style:italic;font-size:16.5px">“{s.diet.confirmed.text}”</p>
    <p style="margin-top:12px">{s.diet.confirmed.en}</p>
    <p style="margin-top:12px"><strong>{s.diet.confirmed.why}</strong></p>
    <p class="cap" style="margin-top:12px">{s.diet.confirmed.also}</p>
  </div>
  <div style="margin-top:24px"><Plates ids={["igp-1895-p1","igp-1895-p2"]} /></div>
  <p class="cap" style="margin-top:14px">{s.diet.source}</p>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <h2>{s.umago.heading}</h2>
  <p class="dek" style="margin-top:10px">{s.umago.lead}</p>
  <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:18px">
    <table><tbody>{s.umago.mayors.map((m, i) => (
      <tr><td style="width:44px">{i + 1}</td><td><strong>{m.n}</strong></td><td>{m.note}</td></tr>
    ))}</tbody></table>
  </div>
  <p class="prose" style="margin-top:16px">{s.umago.count}</p>
  <p class="prose" style="margin-top:14px">{s.umago.after}</p>

  <div class="one" style="border-left-color:var(--accent);margin-top:26px">
    <div class="lab">A collector of unpublished manuscripts</div>
    <h3>{s.umago.historian.heading}</h3>
    <p style="margin-top:10px">{s.umago.historian.text}</p>
    <p style="margin-top:12px"><strong>{s.umago.historian.why}</strong></p>
  </div>

  <div class="one" style="border-left-color:var(--terra);margin-top:18px">
    <div class="lab">Verteneglio, 1775 and 1819</div>
    <h3>{s.umago.woods.heading}</h3>
    <p style="margin-top:10px">{s.umago.woods.text}</p>
    <p style="margin-top:12px">{s.umago.woods.then}</p>
  </div>
  <p class="cap" style="margin-top:18px">{s.umago.source_umago}</p>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <h2>{s.dossier.heading}</h2>
  <p class="dek" style="margin-top:10px">{s.dossier.lead}</p>
  <div style="margin-top:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px">
    {s.dossier.rows.map(r => (
      <div class="one" style={r.key ? "border-left-color:var(--accent)" : ""}>
        <div class="lab">{r.lab}</div>
        <p style="margin-top:8px">{r.text}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="one" style="border-left-color:var(--terra);margin-top:26px">
    <div class="lab">L'Istria Agricola, 1927 and 1934</div>
    <h3>{s.dossier.later.heading}</h3>
    <p style="margin-top:10px">{s.dossier.later.text}</p>
    <p style="margin-top:12px">{s.dossier.later.also}</p>
  </div>

  <div class="one" style="border-left-color:var(--accent);margin-top:20px">
    <div class="lab">Il Piccolo di Trieste, 25 November 1897</div>
    <h3>{s.dossier.death.heading}</h3>
    <p style="margin-top:10px">{s.dossier.death.text}</p>
    <div class="qz" style="margin-top:12px">
      <p class="qit">“{s.dossier.death.quote}”</p>
      <p class="qen">{s.dossier.death.en}</p>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:12px"><strong>{s.dossier.death.why}</strong></p>
  </div>

  <p class="prose note" style="margin-top:22px">{s.dossier.candia_note}</p>
  <p class="cap" style="margin-top:14px">{s.dossier.source_dossier}</p>
</section>

  <Lightbox />
  <Sources ids={["puhmajer", "voce", "blasonario", "crsr", "carlo1879", "omisphotos", "anno", "attirovigno", "laricerca", "piccolo", "archiveorg"]} />
</Base>
